<title>FRANCE: French national assembly passes welfare bill.</title>
<headline>French national assembly passes welfare bill.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French National Assembly adopted on Thursday by 110 votes to 47 the centre-right government's social security spending legislation for 1997 that aims to cut the country's welfare deficit.</p>
<p>Socialists and communists opposed the measure.</p>
<p>The measure would reduce the social security deficit to 30.4 billion francs in 1997 from 51.6 billion francs this year by imposing new spending controls and higher excise duties on alcohol and tobacco.</p>
<p>The government hopes to achieve a surplus in 1999.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
